Components -> Basic building blocks of an Angular Application
    {root component is App Component}
    -- consist of html, css and ts files
    -- spec.ts file is for testing purpose.

1. InterPolation 
  - to bind data from component class to html template. It uses double curly braces {{}}.

2. Property binding
  - to bind properties of html using square brackets []  e.g: [src],[href],[attr] etc
  - Property binding is more reliable for non-binding strings like booleans.

3. Event Binding:(One Way Binding)
  Events are the actions performed by the users
  Types of Events
    1.Mouse Events, 2. Keystroke Events 3. Input Events
  Events are generally executed with the combination of functions

  Note: With Javascript we use onClick() Event
             Angular we use click() Event

  3.1 Mouse Related Events:
  (click)                      (dblclick) - double click
  (mouseover)                  (mouseleave)
  (mousedown)                  (mouseup)
  (drag)                       (dragover)

  3.2 Keyboard Related Events:
  (keypress)                     (Keydown)              (keyup)          (keydown.enter)            (keyup.enter)
  (select)                       (focus)                (input)
  Some more are :
  (copy)                          (cut)               (blur)                  (paste)

  3.3 Event Object
      Event Object($event) in Angular is a reserved keyword that is used to pass the evnet object from template to component typescript file.
  
  